Hi.  I have a question about the rationale behind one aspect of nethack.
Please don't think of this as a gripe (I think the game is a lot of fun
even if I'm not very good at it).

The thing I'm curious about is:  If you attempt to read a spellbook and you
fail for whatever reason (low intelligence, low power, etc), why do you lose
the spellbook.  Just from a pragmatic perspective, where does it go?  Doesn't
it make more sense to just temporarily lower your power rating or something
like that?  Even if you didn't find out what the spellbook was by trying to
read it, you would still have more chances to read it once your power and/or
intelligence went up.

Just curious,
